@startuml simulation-plant-system
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam linetype ortho

title truST Simulation Plant System: Scan And Ownership Boundaries

package "VS Code extension" {
  component "Plant contract +\nmodel descriptors" as plant_contract
  component "Devices & Connections\ngraph shell" as device_graph
  component "Add/configure workflow\nmain-area plant setup" as plant_drawer
  component "Model response / Connections /\nStarting conditions / Optional effects" as plant_sections
  component "PlantModelSchematic\nqualitative themed SVG" as plant_schematic
  component "Optional teaching example\nphysical wording / exact parameter mapping" as plant_example
  component "Indexed port bindings\nmodel cardinality / ownership validation" as plant_ports
  component "Labelled starting-state fields\ncanonical index / finite raw-input guard" as plant_starting
  component "PlantOptionalSettings\none selected task / configured summaries" as plant_optional
  component "Project plant repository\natomic save/remove + revision" as plant_repo
  component "Runtime plant client\nstatus + trace" as plant_client
  component "Stopped-project session\nJSON-lines correlation" as offline_client
  component "Typed Control Studio\nhandoff" as plant_handoff
}

component "Live control transport" as live_transport
plant_sections --> plant_ports : named command / feedback rows
plant_sections --> plant_schematic : selected model identity + purpose
plant_ports --> plant_contract : same canonical draft\npreserve channel order and conversions
plant_sections --> plant_starting : model-specific starting conditions
plant_starting --> plant_contract : same initial-state vector\nno unit or dynamics conversion
plant_sections --> plant_optional : actuator / conversions / realism / scenarios
plant_optional --> plant_contract : read canonical draft summaries\nno secondary settings state
component "trust-runtime plant serve\nstopped-project producer" as offline_transport
component "Shared plant handler\nPlantHandlerContext" as plant_operations
component "PlantControlService\nrevision + idempotency" as plant_service
component "Scheduler command boundary\nstatus / trace / scoped clear" as scheduler_boundary
component "config.set\nsimulation.time_scale\nrefused without simulation" as config_speed
component "Control status\nsimulation_time_scale +\nsimulation_achieved_time_scale" as status_speed
component "RuntimeMetrics\nper-resource achieved speed" as metrics_speed

component "PLC program\nControl.PID" as plc
component "Process image\n%Q command / %I feedback" as io
component "Program storage\nunaddressed command / read-only feedback variables" as program_storage
component "Controller measurement\npid:<instance> feedback, given to that\nControl.PID's Update as Input.ProcessValue" as controller_measurement
component "SimulationController\npre/post-cycle orchestration" as simulation
note right of simulation
Model-structure teaching project: the existing continuous state-space
model owns water and probe deviations, input delay and initial history.
Binding offsets preserve the 35 C / 75% operating point; model-coordinate
actuator limits map to physical 0..100% heating. ST reads both native
temperatures through ordinary PLC inputs and does not emulate the probe.
end note
component "Launch safety gate\nreject physical I/O drivers" as safety
component "Status + bounded trace" as observability

package "PlantSystem" {
  component "Validated plant instance\nstate + fixed-step accumulator" as plant
  component "Typed numeric I/O\nchecked conversion + atomic batch" as numeric
  component "Scheduled events" as events
  component "Command and actuator effects" as actuator
  component "Shared bounded input history\nscalar / continuous state-space channel delays\nchecked aggregate capacity before allocation" as input_history
  component "Nominal model" as model
  component "Parameter, state, output,\nand measurement uncertainty" as uncertainty
  component "Model-validity bounds\ninput + state + output" as validity
  component "Preallocated checkpoint\nfailed-substep rollback" as checkpoint
}

package "Simulation time (spec 33 §6.1)" as simTime {
  component "Resource loop\nrunner_loop.rs: each cycle paced at\ncycle interval / time_scale; pause, resume\nand a speed change restart the schedule" as sim_loop
  component "CycleTiming\ncycle_timing.rs: one exact step per\nexecuted cycle; wall clock without simulation" as sim_timing
  component "SimulationSpeed\nshared time_scale 1..100\nnew speed applies from the next cycle" as sim_speed
  component "AchievedSpeedWindow\nsimulation span / wall span over the\nlast 5 s, reported after 1 s of wall time" as sim_achieved
  component "VS Code simulator\ntrust-debug SimulatorClock\nsame pacing and achieved-speed rules" as vscode_sim
}

note right of sim_timing
Simulation time is the runtime's process time while simulation
is enabled. Wall-clock time and CPU duration do not enter plant
equations. A zero cycle interval reads the scaled wall clock.
end note

safety --> simulation : permits nonphysical drivers only
plant_contract --> device_graph : typed topology state
plant_contract --> plant_drawer : descriptors + validation\nresolve omitted starting state; preserve omission on save
plant_drawer --> plant_sections : one draft and validation state
plant_sections --> plant_example : explicit example choice and replacement review
plant_example --> plant_contract : same canonical draft; no browser physics
plant_drawer --> plant_repo : validate / atomic save or remove
device_graph --> plant_client : current status request
plant_client --> live_transport : bounded typed request
plant_repo --> offline_client : stopped-project read / validate / save / remove
offline_client --> offline_transport : correlated JSON lines
live_transport --> plant_operations : runtime context
offline_transport --> plant_operations : project context
plant_operations --> plant_service : serialize project mutation
plant_operations --> scheduler_boundary : immutable query / explicit clear
plant_service --> plant_operations : replay or apply once
scheduler_boundary --> simulation : scheduler-owned access
device_graph --> plant_handoff : project/runtime/plant/loop identity
plc --> io : commits command during scan
io --> simulation : post-cycle held command
program_storage --> simulation : post-cycle held command (symbolic path)
simulation --> plant : elapsed simulation time
events --> plant : due actions before substep
plant --> actuator : command uncertainty first
actuator --> model : undelayed process input
actuator --> input_history : configured transport delay
input_history --> model : held channel inputs\nsplit existing RK4 steps at delayed boundaries
actuator --> validity : check applied input
actuator --> numeric : optional applied-input feedback\ninverse binding scale; previous completed substep
note right of numeric
Applied feedback shares byte-range ownership checks with
plant, coupling and physics inputs. Reset and fault paths
retain one atomic next-scan publication boundary.
end note
uncertainty --> model : effective parameters
model --> uncertainty : state and ideal output
uncertainty --> validity : check completed state + ideal output
validity --> checkpoint : fail outside local model region
uncertainty --> plant : completed measurement
plant --> checkpoint : save before substep
checkpoint --> plant : restore on fault
checkpoint --> input_history : same substep rollback boundary
plant --> numeric : queue complete feedback
numeric --> simulation : checked encoded batch
simulation --> io : next pre-cycle atomic publication
simulation --> program_storage : then symbolic feedback, all values checked first
simulation --> controller_measurement : held for the scan; cleared with the plant
controller_measurement --> plc : the PID's Update receives it; program variables unchanged
io --> plc : next scan reads feedback
plant --> observability : completed state and fault context
observability --> plant_operations : honest status + bounded trace
live_transport --> config_speed : config.set request
config_speed --> sim_speed : set on the running resource\nfrom the next cycle; never moves time
sim_speed --> sim_loop : speed in force before each cycle
sim_loop --> sim_timing : begin_cycle(wall time, cycle interval)
sim_loop --> simulation : pre-cycle and post-cycle hooks
sim_timing --> simulation : process time of the executed cycle
sim_timing --> sim_achieved : simulation time per wall time
sim_achieved --> metrics_speed : achieved speed published
metrics_speed --> status_speed : read by control status
live_transport --> status_speed : status request
vscode_sim ..> sim_timing : same rules

note right of plant_contract
Transport-independent contract.
No React, filesystem, endpoint,
or executor types.
end note

note right of plant_handoff
Identities and revisions only.
Simulation source is explicit.
No copied live samples.
end note

note right of plant
Each substep commits atomically.
Random streams derive from master seed,
plant ID, and uncertainty ID.
Execution buffers are allocated at activation.
Validity faults roll back; bounds are not safety interlocks.
end note

@enduml
